            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for a guitar, then the Malayalam for a flute."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: താളം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "താളം — tāḷaṁ — \"rhythm; a beat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുട്ടികൾ പാട്ടിന്റെ താളത്തിൽ കൈ കൊട്ടി. kuṭṭikaḷ pāṭṭinṟe tāḷattil kai koṭṭi. The children clapped to the rhythm of the song."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "താളം (tāḷaṁ) തെറ്റുക, to lose the beat, also means to go wrong."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "താളം (tāḷaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit tāla, which CDIAL gives as a cymbal (CDIAL 5801); in Indian music it came to mean the beat the cymbals keep."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
