          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "രാഗം — rāgaṁ — \"a raga; a melody\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആ പാട്ട് ഏത് രാഗത്തിലാണ്? ā pāṭṭŭ ētŭ rāgattilāṇŭ? Which raga is that song in?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A raga is a set of notes and turns that a melody moves within."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "രാഗം (rāgaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit rāga, \"colour, redness\" (CDIAL 10673); Indian music traditionally explains a raga as what colours the listener's mood."
            }
          ]
        },
